# Ixdar Foundation

This rule is the canonical project foundation for AI agents, equivalent to a repository-level `CLAUDE.md`.

## Core Intent

- Keep behavior correct first; preserve existing user-facing behavior unless change is explicitly requested.
- Prefer small, validated increments over large sweeping edits.
- Make each task compound: leave reusable knowledge and safer defaults behind.

## Source of Truth

- Coding conventions and architecture: `ixdar-coding-standards.mdc`
- Ticket lifecycle updates: `ticket-lifecycle.mdc`
- Workflow system: `workflow-plan.mdc`, `workflow-work.mdc`, `workflow-review.mdc`, `workflow-compound.mdc`
- Git safety: `git-safety.mdc`

## Workflow Contract

For non-trivial tasks, follow:

1. Plan
2. Work
3. Review
4. Compound

## Practical Defaults

- Avoid destructive git/shell operations unless explicitly approved.
- Validate with targeted tests whenever feasible.
- Record reusable learnings in `.cursor/docs/ai-learnings/` after significant work (YAML frontmatter required -- see template).
- **Rules vs hooks:** Rules are guidance (agents may skip them). Hooks are enforcement (fire at the platform level every time). Use hooks for any side effect that must happen deterministically (e.g. regenerating board after ticket edit). Use rules for patterns you want agents to follow but can tolerate occasional misses.

## Automation Testing Backbone

- Use `tools/ixdar-automation-cli/ixdar_cli.py` as the default backbone for iterative game/UI testing.
- Prefer CLI-driven checks (`health`, `ui-state`, `start-new-game`, `click`, `record`, `replay`) over ad hoc manual clicking.
- Launch desktop game runs from `ixdar-app/` via `mvn -P game` so runtime flags stay aligned with `.vscode/launch.json` (`-enableassertions`, `sun.awt.noerasebackground`, `org.lwjgl.util.DebugLoader`).
- During automation validation, operate on a single app window/process and verify state transitions through CLI responses.
- Enforce one-app-instance-per-workspace while validating automation. Before launching, confirm existing Ixdar processes and stop extras to avoid port collisions and stale state.
- Treat automation and other background services as lifecycle-managed resources: when wiring startup, also add explicit shutdown so closing the window releases ports and exits cleanly. Prefer `python tools/ixdar-automation-cli/ixdar_cli.py shutdown` for deterministic teardown.
- For runtime asset loading used by audio/gameplay, prefer Maven-packaged classpath resources included in the jar. Use environment variables only for build-time asset ingestion, not runtime resolution.
- For build-ingested runtime assets, prefer property-driven Maven glob includes (e.g. `**/*.wav`) over per-file entries so content can grow without repeated POM edits.